cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this result, please cite the tagged release.
title: "How many starts can be prescribed in two theta prime races?"
abstract: "For every real height from 13450 through 13490 chosen in advance, two further disjoint doublings realize every target in a four-dimensional box of the 547/727 and 571/599 prime races. The finite theorem uses direct prime counts. With starts 2457 and 13471 fixed, the best possible error in the balanced target over disjoint third starts through 300000 is 0.002274350938622389..., with a unique optimizer. For two fixed starts and a third in a nonempty finite union of compact intervals of positive heights, every target has a best fit in a single extension of the input field of degree at most two. Near balance the optimal height generically attains degree two for the specified integer pair. Whole intervals of prescribed heights recur with bounded multiplicative waiting if the nontrivial zeros of the sixteen primitive odd Dirichlet L-functions lie on the critical line."
